  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-unital-associative-algebra-representation": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $k$ be a field, let $A$ be a unital associative $k$-algebra\n([[def-algebra-over-a-commutative-ring]]), and let $V$ be a $k$-vector space.\nWrite $\\operatorname{End}_k(V)=\\mathcal L_k(V,V)$ for the $k$-linear endomorphisms\nof $V$ ([[def-vector-space-of-linear-maps]]); its multiplication is composition\nand its identity is $\\operatorname{id}_V$\n([[def-endomorphism-ring-of-a-module]], [[prop-endomorphisms-form-a-ring]]).\nAn **(unital) representation of $A$ on $V$** is a $k$-linear map\n$$\\rho:A\\longrightarrow\\operatorname{End}_k(V)$$\nsuch that $\\rho(1_A)=\\operatorname{id}_V$ and\n$$\\rho(ab)=\\rho(a)\\circ\\rho(b)\\qquad(a,b\\in A).$$\nThe associated action is $a\\cdot v:=\\rho(a)(v)$. The zero vector space is\nallowed; in that case $\\operatorname{id}_V=0$."
    ],
    "thm-associative-algebra-representations-are-unital-modules": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $k$ be a field, $A$ a unital associative $k$-algebra, and $V$ a\n$k$-vector space. There is a bijection between unital representations\n$\\rho:A\\to\\operatorname{End}_k(V)$ of [[def-unital-associative-algebra-representation]]\nand $k$-bilinear left $A$-module actions $A\\times V\\to V$, $(a,v)\\mapsto a\\cdot v$,\nfor which $(ab)\\cdot v=a\\cdot(b\\cdot v)$ and $1_A\\cdot v=v$. The maps are\n$a\\cdot v=\\rho(a)(v)$ and $\\rho(a)(v)=a\\cdot v$. Here $k$-bilinear means\nlinear in each variable with respect to the given $k$-vector structures; the\nmodule axioms are those of [[def-left-and-right-modules]]."
    ],
